  "notes": "The Booga Basement hybrid: a programmed boom-bap core with a live band and three voices trading over it. Three parameters carry the research. `structure` is `call_response` because the verses are traded and the harmony stacks are structural rather than decorative — which is also why `countermelody.densityRatio` is 0.62, the highest on this axis. The bass is \"dub-loud, with genuine melodic lines and space\": `independent_riff` at `followRootsProb` 0.48, the loosest here, with a `glideProb` of 0.12 for the dub slide. And `modes` is authored rather than inherited, which replaces the archetype's dusty/jazzy/hard set — the research names a reggae one-drop as \"the section's clearest half-time exception\", and a mode is the only place a snare can move to beat 3 without moving it on every seed. ⚠ `confidence` is medium because the research rates this medium-high: multiple producer interviews, but no numbers. ⚠ The INFERRED parameters are the three mode weights and the hat densities — the research says one-drop happens \"on some cuts\" and gives no proportion, so 2 against 4 and 3 is this author's reading, and it is the first thing to correct if the one-drop shows up too often. The percussion lane list (congas, bongos, timbale) is inferred from \"live percussion\" with no instrument named.",
